Dr. Joram Aniya, Member, NITI Aayog, visited Gyekar Sinyik (Ganga Lake) in Arunachal Pradesh to assess its potential for sustainable eco-tourism and discuss measures to strengthen climate resilience and disaster preparedness. Senior officials from NITI Aayog, NDMA, the Central Water Commission, and other concerned agencies were also present.



The visit included discussions with local officials and communities on the need for scientific studies of the lake's hydrology, geology, and catchment dynamics to better understand changing water levels and inform long-term risk mitigation strategies. The delegation also explored sustainable and technically feasible measures to preserve the lake's ecological integrity while reducing disaster risks.



Dr. Joram Aniya emphasised the importance of balancing environmental conservation with scientific planning and community well-being to promote sustainable development in ecologically fragile regions. The visit reaffirmed NITI Aayog's commitment to advancing climate resilience, ecological stewardship, and sustainable tourism in line with the vision of Viksit Bharat.



