Dr. Joram Aniya, Member, NITI Aayog, called on Shri Pema Khandu, Chief Minister of Arunachal Pradesh, during her visit to the State to discuss key priorities for sustainable development, and long-term growth.



The discussions focused on enhancing disaster preparedness and resilient infrastructure while exploring collaboration in school education, tourism, culture, youth affairs, and sports. Emphasis was laid on integrating disaster risk reduction into development planning and addressing the unique geographical and climatic challenges of the North Eastern States.



Dr. Joram Aniya also proposed organising a National Workshop on Sustainable Tourism in Arunachal Pradesh in November 2026 to promote community-based tourism, showcase the State’s rich cultural and natural heritage, and unlock new avenues for sustainable economic growth. Shri Pema Khandu welcomed the proposal and appreciated the continued support of NITI Aayog and NDMA in advancing a resilient and sustainable Arunachal Pradesh in line with the vision of Viksit Bharat.



